":"\n"},{"tag":"script","hidden":true},{"tag":"#text","text":"\n\n"},{"tag":"script","hidden":true},{"tag":"#text","text":"\n\n"},{"tag":"script","hidden":true},{"tag":"#text","text":"\n"},{"tag":"script","hidden":true},{"tag":"#text","text":"\n\n"},{"tag":"script","hidden":true},{"tag":"#text","text":"\n\n"},{"tag":"script","hidden":true},{"tag":"#text","text":"\n\n"},{"tag":"script","hidden":true},{"tag":"#text","text":"\n\n\n\n"},{"tag":"div","hidden":true,"id":"alia-root-324104"}]}]},"canonicalText":"\n\n\n  Skip to main content\n🇺🇸 Labor Day: 20% off all tests—save up to $340. Ends Sept 8. Use code LABORDAY26\n\nProviders\nBecome a Provider\n\nOur TestsAbout TruAgeAbout TruHealthResourcesClinical Case StudiesReport EducationIntervention TrackingIndividuals\nPatientsShop All TestsTruHealth + TruAgeTruHealthTruAgePartners\nOur ServicesResearch ServicesCommercial ServicesWork With Us\n\nOur Science\nScienceOur LaboratoryWhat is epigenetics?Our ArraysIntervention TrackingAlgorithmsOMICmAgeSYMPHONYAgeDunedinPACEOur Publications\n\n\n\nLog In\n\nProvidersBecome a ProviderAbout TruAgeAbout TruHealthClinical Case StudiesReport EducationIntervention TrackingIndividualsShop All TestsTruHealth + TruAgeTruHealthTruAgePartnersResearch ServicesCommercial ServicesWork With UsOur ScienceOur LaboratoryOur ArraysIntervention TrackingDNA MethylationOMICmAgeSYMPHONYAgeDunedinPACEOur Publications\n\n\nAGING SPEEDDunedinPACE™Learn how fast you’re aging. Unlock insights into your aging speed and how you can slow it down.For Providers\n\nFor Individuals\n\n  \n\n\n\n\nspeed of agingDEVELOPED WITH DUKEUnderstand Your Aging SpeedOur DunedinPACE science, developed with Duke, measures how quickly your body ages over time. By monitoring whether your aging speed is accelerating or decelerating, you can measure the effect of various lifestyle changes. Your aging speed, combined with your biological age, empowers you to take proactive steps to optimize your health.Download TruAge Sample Report\n\nIs Your Lifestyle Slowing Your Aging Speed?The DunedinPACE report lets you see the real impact of your lifestyle choices on your aging process. Whether it’s diet, exercise, or sleep, our test provides concrete data on how these factors influence your pace of aging. Routine testing allows you to quickly measure the effects of your habits.Purchase Test Kit\n\nWhy Physicians Trust DunedinPACETM\n\nExplore core diagnostics, reporting tools, and research platforms trusted by leading clinicians and scientists.Real-Time FeedbackQuickly see the results of your lifestyle changes.Advanced TechnologyThe only third-generation biological clock aging algorithm available.Accurate & SensitiveDetect subtle changes in your aging process.Comprehensive ReportsGet detailed insights into your biological responsiveness, lifestyle, and more.BERLIN AGING STUDY IIDunedinPACE is the strongest individual predictor of all-cause mortality.In a 7.4-year study of 1,083 older adults, our pace of aging clock outperformed 14 leading longevity biomarkers — including inflammation markers, grip strength, and cognitive tests.Read the Research\n\nAboutAbout UsHelp CenterCareersNewsletterPartnersBecome a ProviderBecome an AffiliateResearch ServicesRequisition FormAPI ReferenceMembersLog InRegister My KitView My ReportsReturn PolicyCONTACT881 Corporate Dr. Lexington, KY 40503(888) 909-3634Mon-Fri 9am-7pm | Sat 9am-3pmEastern Time (UTC-4:00)support@trudiagnostic.comDNAm biomarker outputs are intended to support, not replace, clinical judgment. They should be interpreted within the full clinical context, including history, physical examination, conventional laboratory testing, and imaging studies where clinically indicated. They should not be used as the sole basis for diagnosis or treatment decisions.Terms of ServicePrivacy PolicyFCIO Policy© TruDiagnostic 2026, All Rights Reserved\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n"}],"residuals":[{"code":"CSS_LAYOUT_NOT_EXECUTED","detail":"External styles, script rendering and computed layout are not evaluated; hidden flags cover only declared inert/hidden content. Hidden subtrees are represented only by their inert root placeholder; their original bytes remain in the capture."}]}